{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793482193,"nonce":"wEOqlx/9qIKT+qrsFnvhVDeB+Q8=","title":"text in a foreground element ignored its clip","message":"A cn::combobox popup is a .foreground() element; its option rows painted below the popup, and over the search field while the list was scrolled. Foreground text always passes through GpuPrimitive::from_glyph, which set the clip type to None unless a path clip was named, so the glyph's rect clip (clip_bounds) was dropped. from_glyph now keeps a rect clip unless clip_bounds is the unbounded default.","files":null}]}